Rewritten for Nodecode: the provider profile (id, display name, description,
base URL, key variable, signup page, the chat-completions wire) is the cell's
catalog row, which is what makes /connect offer CoreWeave, /models list its
models and a turn resolve its lane and address; the key is read from
COREWEAVE_API_KEY as the original reads it, and model discovery, which Hermes
does for any provider, becomes the /coreweave command, which reads
GET <base>/models with the key and puts the answer in /models on demand
rather than at load. The endpoint is the section's base_url, so it can be
moved without editing the cell. Left out: Hermes' provider-registry mechanics
(the ProviderProfile object, register_provider, plugin.yaml and the
`hermes plugins` install path, which Nodecode's folder loader does not have),
the original's optional project-attribution example, which is a separate
custom-provider entry there and a providers.coreweave.models entry here, and
its development tooling (scripts/, tests/, the CI workflow), which checks the
Hermes plugin rather than this cell. Nothing is fetched at load, no fallback
model list is invented, and no capability is claimed for a model CoreWeave did
not list.
